.TH AGENT-HOOK-PROMPT-SUBMIT 1 "2026-10-12" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-prompt-submit \- handle prompt-time agent context refresh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-prompt-submit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-prompt-submit
reads a prompt-submit hook JSON payload from standard input and delegates
memory-intent reminders and prompt-time context refresh policy to
.BR "hm hook prompt-submit" .
It then resets once-per-prompt AgentGuard state used by edit and command
guidance. Unless an extension blocks the prompt, a prompt with text also marks
the agent's tmux pane busy with
.BR "term-pane-mark set busy" ,
when that command is installed. It changes the mark only while the agent
process that runs the hook is the pane terminal's foreground program, so an
agent it launches, which inherits the pane but not its terminal, can neither
set nor clear it. A Codex session without a transcript is not tracked: that
covers Codex's in-process background agents (memory consolidation, task
titles), and also a
.B codex exec \-\-ephemeral
run directly in a pane;
.BR agent-hook-stop (1)
clears the mark when the turn ends.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_HOOKS
Set to
.B 0
to disable Hive Memory hook integration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Prompt handling completed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hm (1),
.BR agent-hook-session-start (1),
.BR term-pane-mark (1)
